// error: `<` needs Period to implement `Ord`
// error: expected Duration, found Period
// error: `+` needs two values of one type, not Period and Duration
// error: `+` needs two values of one type, not Time and Period
// error: `*` needs two numbers of one type, not int and Period
// A period has no order (whether a month is longer than 30 days depends on the month), an instant
// takes no period, a period and a duration never mix, a time of day has no arithmetic, and a count
// scales a period only from the right.
import avin.time.{Period, months, now, days, time}

main()
    println(months(1) < Period(0, 30))
    println(now() + months(1))
    println(months(1) + days(1))
    println(time(9, 0) + months(1))
    println(3 * months(1))
